{title: Sweeter as the Years Go By}
{artist: Lelia Morris}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
Of [Eb]Jesus' love that [Ab]sought me when [Eb]I was lost in sin,
of wondrous grace that [F]brought me back, his [Bb]fold to enter in —
of [Eb]heights and depths of [Ab]mercy far [Eb]deeper than the [Cm]sea,
and [Eb]higher than the [Bb]heavens, my [Eb]theme shall [Bb]ever [Eb]be.

Chorus
[Eb]Sweeter as the [Ab]years go [Eb]by, sweeter as the [Bb]years go by:
[Eb]richer, fuller, [Ab]deeper — [Eb]Jesus' love is [Bb]sweeter, sweeter [Eb]as the years go by.
